  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Owen, you're verified. I can see that one of the two beef pho ($15.00) is missing from order Q-7601. You can choose one of two ways to be compensated:\n\n1. **Refund to your Visa ending 4242:** $12.00. Your order had a promo discount, so the pho's $15.00 price is reduced by its $3.00 share of that discount. The $3.00 is added to your account as credit instead.\n2. **Account credit only:** $18.00, which is the pho's price plus 20%.\n\nWhich would you prefer?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Hmm, I'm not sure about that. I'd rather have the money back on my card, so option 1 is closer to what I want. But why does the promo take $3 off the pho? I only remember using a welcome code, and I don't remember how much it was for. Can you tell me what the discount was?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Your WELCOME10 code took $10.00 off the order's $50.00 subtotal. That's 20% off, spread across all the items in proportion to their price.\n\nThe pho is $15.00 of the $50.00 subtotal, so its share of the discount is $15 \u00d7 $10 \u00f7 $50 = $3.00. You didn't pay that $3.00 for the pho. If I refunded the full $15.00 to your card, you'd get back more than you paid for it.\n\nWith option 1 you'd get:\n- **$12.00 refunded to your Visa ending 4242.** This is what you actually paid for the pho.\n- **$3.00 in account credit** for the promo share, which you can use on a future order.\n\nShould I go ahead with option 1?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I didn't realize the promo was spread across the items. I'm fine with the $12 back on my card and the $3 credit, so yes, go ahead with option 1."
  }
